# This file is the context filter for the released image built by
# .github/workflows/build-docker-image.yml from the Dockerfile at the repository
# root.  It is also read by any other build whose context is this repository --
# including each per-paper artifact's own `docker build -f <dir>/Dockerfile ..`.
# Those two uses want opposite things: the released image wants the artifact
# directories out, and an artifact whose Dockerfile does `COPY . ` wants its own
# directory in, or the experiment scripts its README names are missing from the
# image it produces (the build still succeeds, because copying a directory that
# is not in the context is not an error -- this went unnoticed for a year in two
# packages).  The two uses are kept apart by giving those artifacts their own
# filter: BuildKit reads `<path-to-dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to
# this file, so `cav26ae/Dockerfile.dockerignore` and
# `icfp24ae/Dockerfile.dockerignore` exclude everything below except the one
# directory their build needs, and nothing here changes.  A per-Dockerfile
# filter REPLACES this file rather than adding to it, so each copy repeats the
# rest of these lines.  Docker's rule: patterns apply in order, the last match
# wins, and a pattern matching a directory excludes everything below it.

.git
_build
.vscode

cav21ae_dt
cav21ae_rel
popl24ae
icfp24ae
oopsla25ae
pldi26ae_lower
pldi26ae_omega
